        "uuid": "327449b0_a01a3581",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2209,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T16:57:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this needs to be called when source-\u003esnk connection is stable. pe_snk_hard_reset_exit is just saying the hard reset message has been sent.  Way too early to tell the TCPC to reconnect AutoDischargeDisconnect.  Also don\u0027t think we want to allow disconnects on the TC connection until this point.",
      "parentUuid": "56bcb191_b7e293e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2208,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2209,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e05ab625_27cb43eb",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2209,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T17:10:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The line above is clearing the hard_reset_counter... which is the place the PE has determined we are beyond the hard reset retry sequence.  Seems like it is an OK place to say we are good to go.",
      "parentUuid": "327449b0_a01a3581",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2208,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2209,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a369a56_428c90fa",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2209,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T17:17:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is resetting the counter for a multiple hard resets, but each hard reset even should be independent event and should mark the hard reset complete.\n\nSo if we call N hard_reset_start, I would excepted N hard_reset_complete calls.",
      "parentUuid": "e05ab625_27cb43eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2208,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2209,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1bb99323_a460df83",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2209,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T18:00:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re aiming to ignore Vbus in the TC until its come back, then we should do this in wait_for_capabilities_entry.  I believe in that state we expect Vbus to be stable.",
      "parentUuid": "7a369a56_428c90fa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2208,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2209,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
