        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T16:44:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can you describe the difference between these two flags?\n\nI think TC_FLAGS_HARD_RESET is like TC_FLAGS_HARD_RESET_REQUESTED\n\nand they are mutually exclusive to be set at the same time, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fb6c25c_297007b9",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T16:57:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no. TC_FLAGS_HARD_RESET indicates we are starting the hard reset sequence.  The TC_FLAGS_HARD_RESET_IN_PROGRESS is used to stop the TC state machine from going to unattached like we do with PR_SWAP",
      "parentUuid": "c89c57f9_4cb1cfa6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "200bbbdb_d367eab2",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T17:17:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "line 1850 looks for the hard_reset flag, then clears it and sets the in progress flag. This definitely like it is asking the state machine to start the hard reset process (and that is has not started yet) while the in progress flag indicates that we have already started the hard reset process and haven\u0027t finished yet.\n\n\nIf this is an incorrect understanding, then we definitely need comments explaining how these two flags interact and are different and what they mean",
      "parentUuid": "7fb6c25c_297007b9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec8d10ae_d48a4295",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T17:26:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you think about adding a new TC state for hard reset?\nIt feels like we might be using flags to solve something which should be a separate state?\nIt might be a project for a future CL, but wanted to get your thoughts.",
      "parentUuid": "200bbbdb_d367eab2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57059aaa_0e7c0f93",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T18:00:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would be a deviation from the spec. The TC spec specifically calls out: \n\nA port that is not a V CONN -Powered USB Device and is not in the process of a USB PD\nPR_Swap or a USB PD Hard Reset or a USB PD FR_Swap shall transition to Unattached.SNK\nwithin tSinkDisconnect when V BUS falls below vSinkDisconnect for V BUS operating at or\nbelow 5 V or below vSinkDisconnectPD when negotiated by USB PD to operate above 5 V.\n\nSo we\u0027d have to decide if this is a case where we want to allow such a deviation (like we did for LPM and auto toggle)",
      "parentUuid": "ec8d10ae_d48a4295",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e1b629d_bf94ce59",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-29T18:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain more what would be a deviation? I\u0027m not understanding from reading that section. It says \"and is not in the process of a ... USB PD Hard Reset\", which to me seems compatible with adding a state to track being in the process of a hard reset.",
      "parentUuid": "57059aaa_0e7c0f93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "7b3ff7df0728ff12d8b8ba8982e179398d065be1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
